---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../utils/url";
const layers = [
  ["Data model", "Six integrated classes for policies, rules, numeric ranges, actions, persistent event logs and dispatch runtime, connected through native CMDBuild domains and lookup taxonomies."],
  ["Database engine", "PL/pgSQL functions and triggers for semantic formula validation, range integrity, automatic evaluation of MeterReading data and event lifecycle management."],
  ["Application dispatch", "A Waterway pipeline that claims dispatchable events, builds structured payloads and routes configured actions to notifications or corrective and preventive maintenance processes."],
  ["Interface and analytics", "Dedicated navigation, dynamic showIf forms and reading/consumption dashboards that make configuration and operational behaviour understandable."],
];
const results = ["Invalid formulas, inactive-rule references and inconsistent or overlapping ranges were blocked.","A matching reading opened a traceable ThresholdEventLog linked to its asset, policy and measurement context.","Repeated readings updated the existing open event instead of creating duplicates.","A return to normal conditions automatically closed the event and updated its runtime state.","Configured events successfully generated notifications and started maintenance-process instances."];
---
<BaseLayout title="Threshold-Based Maintenance for openMAINT | Riccardo Paravano" description="Case study of a threshold-based maintenance module developed for openMAINT and CMDBuild.">
  <article class="container page case-study">
    <a class="back" href={withBase("/projects/")}>â† All projects</a>
    <header class="case-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">Enterprise software and databases</p><h1>Threshold-Based Maintenance for openMAINT</h1><p class="lead">During my internship at PAT, part of the Zucchetti Group, I designed, implemented and experimentally validated an integrated subsystem that converts technical asset readings into interpretable events, notifications and maintenance workflows.</p></div><aside><span>Context</span><strong>BSc experimental thesis and internship</strong><span>Platform</span><strong>openMAINT / CMDBuild</strong><span>Core stack</span><strong>PostgreSQL, PL/pgSQL, Waterway</strong></aside></header>
    <section><p class="eyebrow">Problem</p><h2>Turn measurements into governed maintenance decisions.</h2><p>A numeric reading is useful only when it is connected to an asset, a measurement type, a unit, evaluation rules and operational consequences. The module therefore treats a threshold as a configurable domain object rather than an isolated comparison, supporting multiple rules, Boolean policy expressions, traceable event states and automatic actions.</p></section>
    <section><p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p><div class="layer-grid">{layers.map((layer, index) => <div class="layer"><span>0{index + 1}</span><h3>{layer[0]}</h3><p>{layer[1]}</p></div>)}</div></section>
    <section class="split"><div><p class="eyebrow">My contribution</p><h2>From requirements to a working, testable subsystem.</h2></div><div><p>I translated functional, configurability, integrity, observability and integration requirements into a relational model aligned with CMDBuild conventions. I implemented database-side validation and runtime behaviour, separated persistent domain events from dispatch state, connected the engine to Waterway and configured the module within the openMAINT interface.</p><p>The evaluation engine is triggered by new MeterReading records. It identifies applicable policies, filters active rules by measurement type and unit, matches values against configured ranges, resolves the Boolean expression, and then opens, updates or closes the corresponding event. New events can be dispatched to notification templates or maintenance workflows.</p></div></section>
    <section><p class="eyebrow">Validation</p><h2>Verified across configuration, runtime and application behaviour.</h2><ul class="results">{results.map((result) => <li>{result}</li>)}</ul></section>
    <section class="outcome"><p class="eyebrow">Result</p><h2>An interpretable and extensible condition-based maintenance foundation.</h2><p>The final module is integrated rather than external: it uses native classes, domains, lookups, database functions, Waterway gates, menu entries and dynamic forms. The design prioritises transparent rules and controlled configuration while leaving a path toward richer dashboards, additional actions and hybrid predictive techniques.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.case-study{max-width:1120px}.back{display:inline-block;margin-bottom:3rem;color:var(--muted);font-weight:750}.case-header{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.45fr) minmax(16rem,.55fr);gap:clamp(2rem,7vw,6rem);align-items:end;padding-bottom:5rem}.case-header aside{display:grid;gap:.35rem;padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--surface)}.case-header aside span{margin-top:.8rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem}.case-header aside span:first-child{margin-top:0}.case-study section{padding:4.5rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.case-study section>p:not(.eyebrow),.split div:last-child p,.outcome p{max-width:76ch;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.05rem}.layer-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.layer{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--surface)}.layer span{color:var(--accent);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:850}.layer h3{margin-top:1rem}.layer p{margin-bottom:0;color:var(--muted)}.split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:clamp(2rem,7vw,6rem)}.results{display:grid;gap:.75rem;max-width:78ch;padding:0;list-style:none}.results li{position:relative;padding:1rem 1rem 1rem 2.8rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.8rem;background:var(--surface)}.results li::before{position:absolute;left:1rem;color:#5ee0a0;content:"âœ“";font-weight:900}.outcome{padding:clamp(2rem,5vw,4rem)!important;border:1px solid var(--border)!important;border-radius:1.4rem;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(142,197,244,.1),var(--surface))}@media(max-width:800px){.case-header,.split,.layer-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.case-header{padding-bottom:3rem}}
</style>